<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<definitions xmlns="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/MODEL/" xmlns:dmndi="https://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20191111/DMNDI/" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DC/" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DMN/20180521/DI/" id="Disposal_or_transfer_route" name="19.4.1 Determine the disposal or transfer route" namespace="http://tim-method.example/utility-wam/1.0" exporter="Utility WAM Industry Process Reference" exporterVersion="2026-08-28">
  <description>Returns where TITLE goes, and names whether 18 CFR 101 or the contract is the authority. It does not re-decide abandon-versus-remove; 19.2.4 settled the physical end-state and this table takes it as an input.

The distinction the table exists to hold: a physical end-state and a title route are independent. Plant abandoned in place has not gone anywhere and the utility still owns it - and the retirement unit is still established and published to the continuing property record at 19.4.3. Getting that wrong leaves retired plant on the books or writes off plant that is still owned.

18 CFR 101 is the FERC Uniform System of Accounts. Definition 34 defines the retirement unit, which is what 19.4.3 names and publishes; the sale, trade and transfer terms themselves are in the contract and this reference states none of them.</description>
  <inputData id="in_endState" name="Physical end-state from 19.2.4"><variable id="in_endState_v" name="Physical end-state from 19.2.4" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_hasValue" name="Material has recoverable or market value"><variable id="in_hasValue_v" name="Material has recoverable or market value" typeRef="boolean"/></inputData>
  <inputData id="in_counterparty" name="Counterparty type"><variable id="in_counterparty_v" name="Counterparty type" typeRef="string"/></inputData>
  <knowledgeSource id="ks_18cfr101" name="18 CFR 101 Uniform System of Accounts, Definition 34 retirement unit; APQC PCF Utilities 10.4.3 Perform sale or trade"><description>Definition 34 is what makes a retirement unit the thing retired against the continuing property record. APQC 10.4.3 is structural precedent for sale and trade; the terms are contractual and are not stated here.</description></knowledgeSource>
  <decision id="d_19_4_1" name="Title route">
    <variable id="d_19_4_1_v" name="Title route" typeRef="string"/>
    <informationRequirement id="ir_d_19_4_1_ks_18cfr101"><requiredInput href="#ks_18cfr101"/></informationRequirement>
    <decisionTable id="d_19_4_1_dt" hitPolicy="FIRST" preferredOrientation="Rule-as-Row">
      <input id="d_19_4_1_i1" label="Physical end-state"><inputExpression id="d_19_4_1_i1_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_endState</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_19_4_1_i2" label="Has recoverable value"><inputExpression id="d_19_4_1_i2_e" typeRef="boolean"><text>in_hasValue</text></inputExpression></input>
      <input id="d_19_4_1_i3" label="Counterparty"><inputExpression id="d_19_4_1_i3_e" typeRef="string"><text>in_counterparty</text></inputExpression></input>
      <output id="d_19_4_1_o" label="Title route" name="Title route" typeRef="string"/>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r1">
        <description>Title does not move - the plant is still owned and, where it is 192.727(c) inactive, still maintained. 19.4.3 STILL publishes the retirement of the unit named under 18 CFR 101 Definition 34. Physical end-state and accounting end-state are different things.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r1_ie1"><text>"abandonInPlaceNoPurge192727b","abandonInPlacePurged192727b","inactiveNotMaintained192727c"</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r1_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r1_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r1_oe"><text>"retainedInPlace"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r2">
        <description>Transfer to another operator. Terms are in the contract. If the asset is a jointly used structure, 19.4.2 notifies 11.1 - the attachers do not move with it automatically.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r2_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r2_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r2_ie3"><text>"otherOperator"</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r2_oe"><text>"transfer"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r3">
        <description>APQC 10.4.3. Sold or traded against other plant; the retirement unit is retired on the completed transfer at 19.4.2, not before.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r3_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r3_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r3_ie3"><text>"thirdParty"</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r3_oe"><text>"sellOrTrade"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r4">
        <description>No recoverable value. Still a retirement unit under 18 CFR 101 Definition 34, and the material still runs through 19.3.1 in case it is PCB or RCRA.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r4_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r4_ie2"><text>false</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r4_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r4_oe"><text>"scrap"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r5">
        <description>Value but no counterparty established. Scrapped, and 19.3.4 assesses whether any of it returns to stock instead.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r5_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r5_ie2"><text>true</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r5_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r5_oe"><text>"scrap"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
      <rule id="d_19_4_1_r6">
        <description>End-state not established. 19.2.4 settles it and this table consumes it.</description>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r6_ie1"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r6_ie2"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <inputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r6_ie3"><text>-</text></inputEntry>
        <outputEntry id="d_19_4_1_r6_oe"><text>"determineManually"</text></outputEntry>
      </rule>
    </decisionTable>
  </decision>
  <dmndi:DMNDI>
    <dmndi:DMNDiagram id="drd_Disposal_or_transfer_route">
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_endState" dmnElementRef="in_endState"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_hasValue" dmnElementRef="in_hasValue"><dc:Bounds x="245" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_in_counterparty" dmnElementRef="in_counterparty"><dc:Bounds x="430" y="420" width="160" height="45"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_d_19_4_1" dmnElementRef="d_19_4_1"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="240" width="180" height="70"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
      <dmndi:DMNShape id="sh_ks_18cfr101" dmnElementRef="ks_18cfr101"><dc:Bounds x="900" y="100" width="160" height="55"/></dmndi:DMNShape>
    </dmndi:DMNDiagram>
  </dmndi:DMNDI>
</definitions>
